Not sure whether your smiley means that you actually know it...

UML is the Unified Modelling Language. A graphical notion to describe
systems (or whatever you like). One part of it are the Use Case diagrams
which Kent showed on the linked page. The use case facility is the most
primitive piece of UML, IMO, and gives a simple overview of actors of a
system (the person in the middle of the graph) and the things the actors
want to do with the system (the oval boxes).

